{"type":"Environment","id":"free_8868cbbfe526-00d43e4d4b1d","meta":{"status":"ready","error":null},"title":"How a Black Hole Bends Light","lane":"free","label":"model-checked","kitVersion":"0.1.0","htmlSha256":"00d43e4d4b1da91d4f4f1eb8032fae910affccc8481cc844aa0d485fb4ebe35b","html":"<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n<meta http-equiv=\"Content-Security-Policy\" content=\"default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline' http://localhost:3001/vendor/; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src data:; font-src http://localhost:3001/vendor/ data:; connect-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none';\">\n\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><title>How a Black Hole Bends Light</title><style>\n:root{--bg:#ffffff;--fg:#2f3a34;--muted:#4f5d57;--accent:#0a776b;--card:#f7f8f4;--border:#d3dace;--bench:#fbfcf8;--try:#8a3340;--step:#6b4aa0;--gold:#8f6100;--goldsoft:#fff8e6;--goldborder:#ecd9a6;color-scheme:light}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){:root:not([data-theme=\"light\"]){--bg:#16201c;--fg:#e9efea;--muted:#a4b2ab;--accent:#16b6a3;--card:#0e1512;--border:#34403a;--bench:#121a16;--try:#f0a3ad;--step:#b9a0e6;--gold:#e8b84a;--goldsoft:#2a2414;--goldborder:#5a4a1c;color-scheme:dark}}\n:root[data-theme=\"dark\"]{--bg:#16201c;--fg:#e9efea;--muted:#a4b2ab;--accent:#16b6a3;--card:#0e1512;--border:#34403a;--bench:#121a16;--try:#f0a3ad;--step:#b9a0e6;--gold:#e8b84a;--goldsoft:#2a2414;--goldborder:#5a4a1c;color-scheme:dark}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}\nbody{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:16px/1.55 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif}\nmain.lab{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:16px;display:grid;gap:14px}\n.kicker{margin:0;font:700 .75rem/1.2 ui-monospace,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent)}\nh1{margin:.2rem 0 .3rem;font-size:1.6rem;line-height:1.2}\nh2{margin:0 0 .4rem;font-size:1rem;letter-spacing:.02em}\n.try{margin:0;padding:10px 14px;border-left:4px solid var(--try);background:var(--card);border-radius:10px}\n.try strong{color:var(--try)}\n.card{background:var(--card);border:2px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:10px 16px}\n.idea{background:var(--goldsoft);border-color:var(--goldborder)}\n.idea h2{color:var(--gold)}\n.idea p{margin:.2rem 0}\n.top{display:grid;gap:14px;grid-template-columns:1fr}\n.steps ol{margin:0;padding-left:1.4rem}\n.steps li{padding-left:2px}\n.predict ul{margin:.2rem 0 .4rem;padding-left:1.2rem}\nsummary{cursor:pointer;min-height:44px;display:flex;align-items:center;font-weight:600;color:var(--accent)}\n.benchrow{display:grid;gap:14px;grid-template-columns:1fr}\n.bench{background:var(--bench);border:2px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:8px;overflow:hidden}\n.bench svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-height:520px;touch-action:none}\n.side{display:grid;gap:12px;align-content:start}\n.readouts{display:grid;gap:10px;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(140px,1fr))}\n.readout{background:var(--card);border:2px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;padding:8px 12px}\n.readout .name{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted)}\n.readout output{display:block;font-size:1.35rem;font-weight:700;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.found{margin:0;border-color:var(--accent)}\n.found:empty{display:none}\n.fine summary{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted)}\n.row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(90px,auto) 1fr;align-items:center;gap:10px;min-height:44px}\n.row label{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted)}\n.row input[type=range]{width:100%;min-height:44px;accent-color:var(--accent)}\n.hints details{border-top:1px solid var(--border)}\n.hints details:first-of-type{border-top:0}\n.explain p{margin:.3rem 0}\n@media (min-width:760px){.top{grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr}.benchrow{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.6fr) minmax(260px,1fr)}}\n\n#bench-art{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;background:var(--bench);border-radius:12px}\n#bench-art .lbl{fill:var(--fg);font-size:13px;font-family:sans-serif}\n#bench-art .sm{fill:var(--muted);font-size:11px;font-family:sans-serif}\n#bench-art .ray{fill:none;stroke:#ffd34d;stroke-width:3;stroke-linejoin:round}\n#bench-art .ref{fill:none;stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:6 6}\n#bench-art .ps{fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:4 4}\n#bench-art .trk{stroke:var(--border);stroke-width:6;stroke-linecap:round}\n#bench-art .star{fill:var(--muted)}</style></head><body><main class=\"lab\"><header><p class=\"kicker\">Physics, Form 4 (Gravitation, going further)</p><h1>How a Black Hole Bends Light</h1><p class=\"try\"><strong>Try this:</strong> Drag the yellow laser on the left up or down to aim its beam closer to or further from the black hole.</p></header><div class=\"top\"><section class=\"card idea\"><h2>Key idea</h2><p>Mass curves space, and light follows that curve, so a beam passing a black hole bends towards it. The closer it passes, and the heavier the hole, the more it bends. Too close, and the light cannot escape at all.</p><p>Far-away estimate: bend angle = 4GM / (c^2 b) = 2 Rs / b, with Rs = 2GM / c^2</p></section><section class=\"card predict\"><h2>Predict first</h2><p>You aim the beam closer and closer to the black hole. What happens to the light?</p><ul><li>It bends by the same amount at every distance</li><li>It bends more and more, then gets captured</li><li>It bends less, because it passes faster</li></ul><details><summary>Check your prediction</summary><p>drag the laser down towards the hole and watch the bend angle readout and the beam.</p></details></section></div><section class=\"card steps\"><h2>Steps</h2><ol><li>Drag the laser to its highest point and look at the beam. It bends only a little away from the dashed no-gravity line.</li><li>Drag the laser slowly down. Watch the bend angle grow, and compare it with the far-away estimate.</li><li>Keep going until the beam loops around the photon sphere and then falls into the black hole.</li><li>Drag the mass knob along the track under the hole. A heavier hole has a bigger horizon and bends the same beam more.</li></ol></section><section class=\"benchrow\" aria-label=\"The lab bench\"><div class=\"bench\"><svg id=\"bench-art\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 380\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A light beam passing a black hole\">\n<defs>\n<radialGradient id=\"glow\"><stop offset=\"0.6\" stop-color=\"#ff9a2e\" stop-opacity=\"0.9\"/><stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#ff9a2e\" stop-opacity=\"0\"/></radialGradient>\n</defs>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"640\" height=\"380\" fill=\"var(--bench)\"/>\n<g id=\"stars\"></g>\n<line id=\"refline\" class=\"ref\" x1=\"60\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"640\" y2=\"120\"/>\n<text id=\"reflbl\" class=\"sm\" x=\"470\" y=\"112\">path with no gravity</text>\n<circle id=\"halo\" cx=\"330\" cy=\"200\" r=\"20\" fill=\"url(#glow)\"/>\n<circle id=\"hole\" cx=\"330\" cy=\"200\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#ff9a2e\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<circle id=\"psph\" class=\"ps\" cx=\"330\" cy=\"200\" r=\"22\"/>\n<path id=\"ray\" class=\"ray\" d=\"M0 0\"/>\n<circle id=\"dot\" cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#fff6c2\"/>\n<text class=\"lbl\" x=\"250\" y=\"22\">Black hole: event horizon (black), photon sphere (dashed)</text>\n<g id=\"laser\" data-synapse-handle=\"aim\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"touch-action:none;cursor:grab\" transform=\"translate(0,120)\">\n<circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"0\" r=\"26\" fill=\"var(--card)\" stroke=\"var(--border)\"/>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"-8\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"var(--fg)\"/>\n<circle cx=\"54\" cy=\"0\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#ffd34d\"/>\n</g>\n<text class=\"sm\" x=\"8\" y=\"370\">Laser: drag up or down</text>\n<line class=\"trk\" x1=\"220\" y1=\"352\" x2=\"440\" y2=\"352\"/>\n<text class=\"sm\" x=\"196\" y=\"356\">1</text>\n<text class=\"sm\" x=\"450\" y=\"356\">20 solar masses</text>\n<text class=\"sm\" x=\"260\" y=\"338\">Mass: drag the knob along</text>\n<circle id=\"knob\" data-synapse-handle=\"mass\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"touch-action:none;cursor:grab\" cx=\"300\" cy=\"352\" r=\"22\" fill=\"var(--accent)\" stroke=\"var(--fg)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n</svg></div><div class=\"side\"><div class=\"readouts\"><div class=\"readout\"><div class=\"name\" id=\"rs-name\">Schwarzschild radius Rs (km)</div><output id=\"rs\" data-synapse-readout=\"rs\" aria-labelledby=\"rs-name\"></output></div><div class=\"readout\"><div class=\"name\" id=\"ratio-name\">Beam distance b in units of Rs</div><output id=\"ratio\" data-synapse-readout=\"ratio\" aria-labelledby=\"ratio-name\"></output></div><div class=\"readout\"><div class=\"name\" id=\"bend-name\">True bend angle (degrees)</div><output id=\"bend\" data-synapse-readout=\"bend\" aria-labelledby=\"bend-name\"></output></div><div class=\"readout\"><div class=\"name\" id=\"est-name\">Far-away estimate 2Rs/b (degrees)</div><output id=\"est\" data-synapse-readout=\"est\" aria-labelledby=\"est-name\"></output></div></div><p id=\"found\" class=\"card found\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p><details class=\"card fine\"><summary>Keyboard controls</summary><div class=\"row\"><label for=\"aim\">Distance of beam from centre, b</label><input type=\"range\" id=\"aim\" data-synapse-control=\"aim\" min=\"10\" max=\"170\" step=\"1\" value=\"120\" data-unit=\"km\" aria-valuetext=\"120 km\"></div><div class=\"row\"><label for=\"mass\">Black hole mass</label><input type=\"range\" id=\"mass\" data-synapse-control=\"mass\" min=\"1\" max=\"20\" step=\"1\" value=\"8\" data-unit=\"solar masses\" aria-valuetext=\"8 solar masses\"></div></details></div></section><section class=\"card hints\"><h2>Need a hint?</h2><details><summary>Hint 1</summary><p>Compare the bend angle with the far-away estimate when the beam passes far from the hole, and again when it passes close.</p></details><details><summary>Hint 2</summary><p>The estimate 2 Rs / b works well when b is many times Rs. Near the hole the true bend grows much faster.</p></details><details><summary>Hint 3</summary><p>When b is less than about 2.6 Rs, the light is captured. Doubling the mass doubles Rs, so the same beam is captured more easily.</p></details></section><section class=\"explain\"><h2>Why it happens</h2><p>Einstein&#x27;s general relativity says mass curves space and time. Light always takes the straightest path it can. In curved space that path bends, so a beam passing a massive object turns towards it. The Sun does this too, but only by about 0.0005 degrees. A black hole packs a huge mass into a tiny size, so light can pass very close and bend by a lot.</p><p>The event horizon has the Schwarzschild radius Rs = 2GM / c^2, about 2.95 km for every solar mass. At 1.5 Rs is the photon sphere, where light can circle the hole. A beam aimed with b less than about 2.6 Rs crosses inside it and spirals in, never to return.</p><p>Far from the hole, the bend is close to 4GM / (c^2 b). Astronomers see this as gravitational lensing: galaxies and black holes act like giant lenses that bend, stretch and multiply the light of objects behind them.</p></section></main><script>\naddEventListener(\"message\", function (e) {\n  var d = e.data;\n  if (d && typeof d === \"object\" && d.type === \"synapse_theme\" && (d.theme === \"light\" || d.theme === \"dark\")) document.documentElement.setAttribute(\"data-theme\", d.theme);\n});\nArray.prototype.forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll(\"input[data-synapse-control]\"), function (el) {\n  function say() { el.setAttribute(\"aria-valuetext\", el.value + (el.dataset.unit ? \" \" + el.dataset.unit : \"\")); }\n  el.addEventListener(\"input\", say);\n  say();\n});\n\n(function () {\nvar svg = document.getElementById(\"bench-art\");\nvar NS = svg.namespaceURI;\nfunction $(id) { return document.getElementById(id); }\nvar aim = $(\"aim\"), mass = $(\"mass\");\nvar CX = 330, CY = 200, S = 1;\nvar G = 6.67e-11, C_MS = 3.00e8, MSUN_KG = 1.99e30;\nvar RS_PER_MSUN_KM = 2 * G * MSUN_KG / (C_MS * C_MS) / 1000;\n\nfunction rsKm(m) { return RS_PER_MSUN_KM * m; }\nfunction weakBendDeg(m, bKm) { return 2 * rsKm(m) / bKm * 180 / Math.PI; }\n\nvar st = $(\"stars\");\nfor (var i = 0; i < 45; i++) {\n  var c = document.createElementNS(NS, \"circle\");\n  c.setAttribute(\"cx\", (i * 137 + 23) % 640);\n  c.setAttribute(\"cy\", (i * 89 + 11) % 380);\n  c.setAttribute(\"r\", 0.6 + (i % 3) * 0.5);\n  c.setAttribute(\"class\", \"star\");\n  st.appendChild(c);\n}\n\nfunction trace(rs, b) {\n  var u = 0, w = 1 / b, phi = 0, h = 0.002;\n  var pts = [[-20, CY - b * S]], cap = true, end = 0;\n  function f(x) { return -x + 1.5 * rs * x * x; }\n  for (var i = 0; i < 40000; i++) {\n    var k1u = w, k1w = f(u);\n    var k2u = w + h / 2 * k1w, k2w = f(u + h / 2 * k1u);\n    var k3u = w + h / 2 * k2w, k3w = f(u + h / 2 * k2u);\n    var k4u = w + h * k3w, k4w = f(u + h * k3u);\n    var nu = u + h / 6 * (k1u + 2 * k2u + 2 * k3u + k4u);\n    var nw = w + h / 6 * (k1w + 2 * k2w + 2 * k3w + k4w);\n    if (nu >= 1 / rs) {\n      phi += h;\n      pts.push([CX - rs * Math.cos(phi) * S, CY - rs * Math.sin(phi) * S]);\n      break;\n    }\n    if (nu <= 0 && i > 0) { end = phi + h * u / (u - nu); cap = false; break; }\n    u = nu; w = nw; phi += h;\n    var r = 1 / u;\n    if (r < 900) pts.push([CX - r * Math.cos(phi) * S, CY - r * Math.sin(phi) * S]);\n  }\n  if (!cap && pts.length > 2) {\n    var a = pts[pts.length - 2], z = pts[pts.length - 1];\n    var dx = z[0] - a[0], dy = z[1] - a[1], L = Math.hypot(dx, dy) || 1;\n    pts.push([z[0] + dx / L * 1500, z[1] + dy / L * 1500]);\n  }\n  return { pts: pts, cap: cap, bendRad: cap ? 0 : end - Math.PI };\n}\n\nfunction update() {\n  var b = Number(aim.value), m = Number(mass.value);\n  var rs = rsKm(m);\n  var t = trace(rs, b);\n  var d = \"M\" + t.pts.map(function (p) { return p[0].toFixed(1) + \" \" + p[1].toFixed(1); }).join(\" L\");\n  $(\"ray\").setAttribute(\"d\", d);\n  $(\"hole\").setAttribute(\"r\", (rs * S).toFixed(1));\n  $(\"halo\").setAttribute(\"r\", (rs * S * 1.6 + 4).toFixed(1));\n  $(\"psph\").setAttribute(\"r\", (1.5 * rs * S).toFixed(1));\n  var y = CY - b * S;\n  $(\"laser\").setAttribute(\"transform\", \"translate(0,\" + y + \")\");\n  $(\"refline\").setAttribute(\"y1\", y); $(\"refline\").setAttribute(\"y2\", y);\n  $(\"reflbl\").setAttribute(\"y\", y - 8);\n  $(\"knob\").setAttribute(\"cx\", 220 + (m - 1) / 19 * 220);\n  var ratio = b / rs, est = weakBendDeg(m, b);\n  var bendDeg = t.bendRad * 180 / Math.PI;\n  $(\"rs\").textContent = rs.toFixed(1) + \" km\";\n  $(\"ratio\").textContent = ratio.toFixed(2) + \" Rs\";\n  $(\"bend\").textContent = t.cap ? \"captured (b below 2.60 Rs)\" : bendDeg.toFixed(1) + \" degrees\";\n  $(\"est\").textContent = est.toFixed(1) + \" degrees\";\n  var s = t.cap\n    ? \"A \" + m + \" solar mass black hole (Rs \" + rs.toFixed(1) + \" km) captures a beam aimed \" + b + \" km from its centre (\" + ratio.toFixed(2) + \" Rs).\"\n    : \"A \" + m + \" solar mass black hole (Rs \" + rs.toFixed(1) + \" km) bends a beam aimed \" + b + \" km away (\" + ratio.toFixed(2) + \" Rs) by \" + bendDeg.toFixed(1) + \" degrees; the far-away estimate is \" + est.toFixed(1) + \" degrees.\";\n  $(\"found\").textContent = s;\n  svg.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", s);\n  if (still) placeDot(0.5);\n}\n\nfunction svgPt(e) {\n  var p = svg.createSVGPoint();\n  p.x = e.clientX; p.y = e.clientY;\n  return p.matrixTransform(svg.getScreenCTM().inverse());\n}\nfunction setCtl(ctl, v) {\n  var mn = Number(ctl.min), mx = Number(ctl.max), sp = Number(ctl.step);\n  v = Math.min(mx, Math.max(mn, v));\n  v = mn + Math.round((v - mn) / sp) * sp;\n  ctl.value = v;\n  ctl.dispatchEvent(new Event(\"input\", { bubbles: true }));\n}\nfunction drag(el, ctl, toVal) {\n  var on = false;\n  el.addEventListener(\"pointerdown\", function (e) {\n    el.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); on = true; setCtl(ctl, toVal(svgPt(e)));\n  });\n  el.addEventListener(\"pointermove\", function (e) { if (on) setCtl(ctl, toVal(svgPt(e))); });\n  el.addEventListener(\"pointerup\", function () { on = false; });\n  el.addEventListener(\"pointercancel\", function () { on = false; });\n}\ndrag($(\"laser\"), aim, function (q) { return (CY - q.y) / S; });\ndrag($(\"knob\"), mass, function (q) { return 1 + (q.x - 220) / 220 * 19; });\naim.addEventListener(\"input\", update);\nmass.addEventListener(\"input\", update);\n\nvar still = window.matchMedia(\"(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)\").matches;\nvar ray = $(\"ray\"), dot = $(\"dot\");\nfunction placeDot(f) {\n  var L = ray.getTotalLength();\n  var p = ray.getPointAtLength(Math.min(L, 900) * f);\n  dot.setAttribute(\"cx\", p.x); dot.setAttribute(\"cy\", p.y);\n}\nfunction frame(ts) {\n  placeDot((ts % 3000) / 3000);\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\nupdate();\nif (still) placeDot(0.5); else requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n})();</script></body></html>","citations":[{"source":"UNVERIFIED (no textbook page has been checked for this Environment)","page":null,"quote":null,"verified":false,"printedPage":null}],"checked":{"layers":["postprocess","scan","render"],"controlsExercised":2,"gridPoints":0,"referenceCases":0,"readouts":4,"models":[],"limits":"Written whole by a model and not built on the Kit, so none of its numbers or formulas were compared with an audited science model. Code checked that it runs and that its controls work, but only for a short, scripted stretch of time. No textbook source was checked and a person has not reviewed it. Check it against your textbook."},"planSummary":"A page written whole by a model for a question the Kit could not express (topic none)."}